<title>BELGIUM: EU to vote Thursday on grain export proof.</title>
<headline>EU to vote Thursday on grain export proof.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union grain officials are due at Thursday's weekly cereals management committee session to vote on a proposal requiring proof of arrival for grain shipments of more than 1,500 tonnes benefiting from differentiated export refunds, EU sources said.</p>
<p>They said that the change to regulation 1501/95 would mainly affect sales to Morocco, Algeria and other North African countries for which special refund rates are set.</p>
<p>&quot;The aim is to improve controls to ensure the grain is delivered to the specified destinations,&quot; one source said.</p>
<p>Vessels carrying less than 1,500 tonnes of grain will continue to have to show proof of arrival.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
